Mark XXII: the Record (session history everywhere)

The Second Mind was CLI-only to read; now every surface can reach it.

- Bridge: GET /api/history (recent sessions) and GET /api/session?id=N
  (one session's messages) - token-gated like every bridge endpoint, so
  the phone can browse desktop conversation history.
- Dashboard: GET /api/session?id=N plus POST /api/resume {id} - the
  browser equivalent of /resume: resets the live agent and loads a
  recorded session back into context, with a status event in the stream.
  Unknown/empty sessions return 404.
- dashboard_page.py: PAST SESSIONS rows gain a RESUME button that loads
  the session into the console and reports it in the event stream.
- Launcher v1.3 (separate repo) consumes the bridge endpoints.
- Tests: bridge history token gate + ordering + message read; dashboard
  session read, resume-into-agent (roles and content verified), 404s.
- Version 3.9.0.
